{
  "text": " Every programmer has a brilliant engineering partner they trust. Codex, Grock, Pi, or Claude code. An idea becomes something you can build together. Once you have your own multi-agent workflow, the real problem becomes management. Who is progressing? Who is blocked and who takes the next step? Herder is the manager for those brilliant individuals It brings workspaces, terminals, and agent status together. But the weekend is here. You should not have to sit at your computer watching progress. Who manages the manager? Hermes on Herter gives that job to a dedicated, trusted Hermes profile on this machine. You're M2, a manager for the manager. This dedicated Hermes has worked for the company full Herder control. It can inspect status, coordinate work, and carry your instructions to the agents doing it. When enabled, it starts with Herder and stops with its session, inside a real pane. A pause stays paused until you explicitly resume. Open the monitor TUI, your synchronously through your configured Hermes messaging platform. Keep the machine in Herter online and step away. Let the system manage the genius. Keep the weekend for yourself. Hermes on Herter by Hex Lea I.",
